<title>POLAND: Bank of NY to deposit Mostostal-E ADRs.</title>
<headline>Bank of NY to deposit Mostostal-E ADRs.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish construction and trading company Mostostal Export SA said in a statement it signed an agreement with Bank of New York to be the Depository bank of the firm's American Depositary Receipts (ADRs).</p>
<p>Mostostal said in Friday's statement the agreement would come into effect on February 17.</p>
<p>It said the trade of the ADRs, representing up to five percent of Mostostal shares, would be carried out in New York and London.</p>
<p>In March last year Mostostal said its shares were transferred to Nomura International Trust Company's account, with Nomura beginning to issue ADRs.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
